{"full":"hf:build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi","spaceId":"build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi","name":"Kirana Saathi","source":"huggingface","description":"Hindi voice + photo inventory & udhaar ledger for kiranas","category":"AI & machine learning","language":null,"topics":["docker","track:backyard","sponsor:modal","sponsor:openbmb","achievement:offbrand","achievement:llama","achievement:sharing","achievement:fieldnotes","region:us"],"technologies":[],"likes":23,"created":"2026-06-15T23:06:19.000Z","updated":"2026-06-15T23:06:31.000Z","license":null,"runtime":"SLEEPING","appUrl":"https://build-small-hackathon-kirana-saathi.hf.space/","demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi","availability":"available","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:41:40.705Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T15:41:40.705Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T15:41:40.705Z","color":"#3c3250","ink":"#e4d4ff","symbol":"🏪","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A Hindi-first assistant for a small kirana (corner) shop. The owner just talks, or shows a photo of a bill, and the app keeps the two things that used to live on paper: the stock, and the udhaar, the running credit customers pay back later. It also watches the shelf, flags what is about to expire or is not selling, suggests a discount to clear slow stock, and reminds the owner to restock before a festival.","Built for the Build Small Hackathon, Backyard AI track. Everything runs on open-weight models, each well under 32B. Understanding and vision come from MiniCPM-V-4.6 (5-6B) by OpenBMB. No proprietary frontier API touches the loop. For this demo the model is reached through OpenBMB's hosted MiniCPM API, while speech runs on Modal and the bill OCR pre-pass runs on llama.cpp (see Hosting)."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"fb5474ff0de819aeba6ae74e847de4c349784667a0d661590386ed37406e47c2","extractedAt":"2026-10-06T15:41:40.822Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T15:41:40.822Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A Hindi-first assistant for a small kirana (corner) shop. The owner just talks, or shows a photo of a bill, and the app keeps the two things that used to live on paper: the stock, and the udhaar, the running credit customers pay back later. It also watches the shelf, flags what is about to expire or is not selling, suggests a discount to clear slow stock, and reminds the owner to restock before a festival.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"Built for the Build Small Hackathon, Backyard AI track. Everything runs on open-weight models, each well under 32B. Understanding and vision come from MiniCPM-V-4.6 (5-6B) by OpenBMB. No proprietary frontier API touches the loop. For this demo the model is reached through OpenBMB's hosted MiniCPM API, while speech runs on Modal and the bill OCR pre-pass runs on llama.cpp (see…","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[{"kind":"hosting","status":"documented","text":"MiniCPM-V-4.6 is small enough to self-host on a single GPU, and the speech models are smaller still, so nothing forces a hosted dependency.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"hosting","status":"optional","text":"Because MiniCPM-V-4.6 also ships an official GGUF, the LLM + vision can be moved to local llama.cpp if you want a fully self-hosted setup.","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"fb5474ff0de819aeba6ae74e847de4c349784667a0d661590386ed37406e47c2","sourceUrl":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/build-small-hackathon/kirana-saathi/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-06T15:41:40.822Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-06-15T23:06:31.000Z",